keywords:
  - Erdős–Szekeres problem
  - convex position
  - points in higher dimensions
  - interior-point certificates
abstract: >-
  Eleven integer points in general position in four-dimensional space with no
  eight in convex position, and fifteen in three-dimensional space with no
  eight in convex position, with certificates that each eight points contain a
  point inside a simplex of others. Hence g(4)(8) is 12 or 13 and
  g(3)(8) >= 16.
